## 4. Authentication & Authorization (RBAC)

### 4.1 Firebase → Backend Token Flow
```
Client sends: Authorization: Bearer <Firebase ID Token>
    │
    ▼
Auth Service (/auth/verify)
    │  1. Check Redis cache (token hash → user obj, TTL 5min)
    │  2. If miss: firebase_admin.auth().verify_id_token(token)
    │  3. Fetch user from PostgreSQL by firebase_uid
    │  4. Return: { user_id, email, role, permissions[] }
    │
    ▼
All other services use Auth Service via internal HTTP or JWT-derived context
```

### 4.2 Roles & Permissions Matrix

| Permission | CANDIDATE | EMPLOYER | SUPER_ADMIN |
|---|---|---|---|
| Browse public jobs | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Apply to jobs | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| View own kanban | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Use AI Hub (ATS) | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ |
| Post jobs | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| View applicants | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Approve/reject jobs | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |
| Manage all users | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ |
| Access analytics | own only | company-level | platform-wide |
| Manage companies | ❌ | own company | ✅ all |

### 4.3 Role Assignment Flow
```python
# POST /auth/register → triggered after Firebase signup
{
  "firebase_token": "...",
  "requested_role": "CANDIDATE" | "EMPLOYER",
  "company_name": "..."    # only if EMPLOYER
}

# Auth Service:
# 1. verify firebase token
# 2. create user in PostgreSQL with role
# 3. create profile skeleton in MongoDB
# 4. If EMPLOYER: create company record (pending verification)
# 5. Emit "user.registered" event to Notification Service
```

