## 12. Concurrency & Performance Design

### 12.1 Async FastAPI throughout
```python
# Every endpoint is async — non-blocking I/O
@router.get("/jobs")
async def get_jobs(filters: JobFilter, db: AsyncMotorDatabase = Depends(get_mongo)):
    async with db["jobs"].find(query).skip(skip).limit(limit) as cursor:
        jobs = await cursor.to_list(length=limit)
    return PaginatedResponse(data=jobs, total=total, page=page)
```

### 12.2 Gunicorn + Uvicorn workers
```bash
# Production: Gunicorn manages multiple Uvicorn async workers
gunicorn app.main:app \
  --worker-class uvicorn.workers.UvicornWorker \
  --workers 4 \                    # (2 × CPU cores)
  --max-requests 1000 \            # worker recycling to prevent memory leaks
  --timeout 60
```

### 12.3 Database Connection Pooling
```python
# PostgreSQL: asyncpg connection pool
engine = create_async_engine(
    DATABASE_URL,
    pool_size=20,
    max_overflow=10,
    pool_pre_ping=True,
    pool_recycle=3600
)

# MongoDB: Motor client (async, connection pool built-in)
motor_client = AsyncIOMotorClient(MONGO_URI, maxPoolSize=50)

# Redis: aioredis connection pool
redis_pool = aioredis.ConnectionPool.from_url(REDIS_URL, max_connections=20)
```

### 12.4 Celery Workers (Heavy tasks off main thread)
```bash
# AI Worker (GPU-friendly tasks)
celery -A ai_service.worker worker \
  --queues=ai_tasks \
  --concurrency=2 \         # limited by OpenAI rate limits + memory
  --prefetch-multiplier=1

# Scraper Worker (I/O heavy, more concurrency)  
celery -A scraper_service.worker worker \
  --queues=scrape_tasks \
  --concurrency=6

# Email Worker
celery -A notification_service.worker worker \
  --queues=email_queue \
  --concurrency=4
```

### 12.5 Caching Strategy
```python
# Redis cache decorator (custom)
@cache(key="jobs:search:{hash(filters)}", ttl=120)  # 2 minutes
async def search_jobs(filters: JobFilter): ...

@cache(key="job:{job_id}", ttl=600)                 # 10 minutes
async def get_job_detail(job_id: str): ...

@cache(key="profile:{user_id}", ttl=300)            # 5 minutes
async def get_candidate_profile(user_id: str): ...

# Cache invalidation on mutation:
await redis.delete(f"job:{job_id}")
await redis.delete_pattern("jobs:search:*")
```

### 12.6 Rate Limiting
```python
# Per-endpoint rate limits (FastAPI middleware)
RATE_LIMITS = {
    "/api/ai/score-resume": "10/hour",      # AI calls expensive
    "/api/ai/chat": "30/hour",              # Chat messages
    "/api/jobs": "100/minute",              # Search
    "/api/auth/register": "5/hour",         # Anti-spam
    "/api/jobs/{id}/apply": "20/hour",      # Anti-abuse
}
```

