## 13. Security Design

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| Auth | Firebase ID Token (RS256) verification on every request |
| Token Caching | Redis with 5min TTL to avoid repeated Firebase calls |
| SQL Injection | SQLAlchemy ORM parameterized queries |
| NoSQL Injection | Pydantic schema validation before any DB query |
| CORS | Strict allowlist: only frontend domains |
| Rate Limiting | Redis sliding window per IP + per user |
| File Upload | MIME type validation, size limit (5MB), virus scan |
| Scraper | IP rotation, user-agent rotation, respect robots.txt |
| Secrets | Environment variables, never committed (python-decouple) |
| HTTPS | TLS via Nginx / Traefik (Let's Encrypt) |
| Audit Log | All admin actions logged to PostgreSQL audit_logs |

