## 18. Open Questions / Design Decisions for Review

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Scraping Legal Compliance** — LinkedIn and Indeed prohibit scraping in their ToS. 
> Recommended: use official LinkedIn Jobs API (requires partner approval) for LinkedIn,
> and/or use only sources that permit scraping. Please confirm which job boards to scrape.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Database Hosting** — For production, do you want:
> - **Self-hosted** (docker on VPS) — lower cost, more ops work
> - **Managed cloud** (MongoDB Atlas + AWS RDS + Redis Cloud) — higher cost, zero ops
> - **Hybrid** — managed DBs, self-hosted services

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: AI Costs** — OpenAI GPT-4o API calls for ATS scoring and chat will incur per-token costs.
> Should we implement a **free tier** (N AI calls/month per user) and **premium tier** (unlimited)?
> Or is AI free for all users initially?

> [!NOTE]
> **Q4: Employer Verification** — When an employer registers, should they be:
> A) Auto-approved (can post jobs immediately)
> B) Manually verified by admin before posting
> C) Email domain verification (match company domain)

> [!NOTE]  
> **Q5: Salary Currency** — Should salary be stored in a single currency (INR) or multi-currency with conversion?

